{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem (resolved during this ticket's lifetime — this ticket now verifies the fix)\n\nEpic `0e68-41eb-5782-4336` (outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast) had a 10,135-character description,\nover the 8,000-char review admission cap (`7cf80009d9`). `review-plan` on the epic returned a single\nblocking P4 admission finding without running the LLM, so the epic could not earn a plan-review\nattestation — and the parent-first claim cascade therefore blocked EVERY child of the epic\n(discovered when `bloated-shadeful-lamprey`'s claim failed with \"Parent error: no certified\nplan-review attestation\").\n\n## State at planning time\n\nThe epic's description has ALREADY been condensed by the session owner: the description field now\nmeasures 7389 characters (under the cap), and the full 10,135-char original is preserved verbatim as\nan epic comment dated 2026-08-13. Editing the epic changes only the epic's OWN material fingerprint —\nchildren's attestations bind their own material (material_diff.material_basis), not the parent's, so\nno sibling attestation was invalidated by the edit.\n\n## Remaining work (verification only; no further edits prescribed)\n\nRun the epic's plan review to earn the certified PASS the cascade requires, then prove the cascade\nis unblocked with a child claim.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `0e68-41eb-5782-4336`'s description field measures at most 8,000 characters; checked by reading the field and reporting the measured length.\n- [ ] `rebar review-plan 0e68-41eb-5782-4336` admits the plan — no P4 admission finding in the result; checked by inspecting the review output's blocking list.\n- [ ] `rebar review-plan 0e68-41eb-5782-4336` returns a certified PASS with zero blocking findings and a persisted, signed plan-review attestation (checked with `--status`; if a PASS fails to persist, `rebar sign-review` is the recovery), before the claim check below.\n- [ ] A child of the epic can be claimed without the parent cascade failing; checked by `rebar claim bloated-shadeful-lamprey` exiting 0 (its own plan-review attestation is already certified and its material unchanged).\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786609989073158001,"uuid":"ca7112db-f41b-4151-be9f-db72ce71964b"}